      "id": 89,
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### What this shows\n\nOne card per switch port, from a **single panel repeated** over the `Port` variable. That variable is a custom `name : state` list, so one entry carries both: its text form names the card (Cluster Name expands template variables) and its value feeds the query with the link state. Adding a port means adding one entry.\n\nThe threshold is **single-sided**: Critical is `0` and Warning is left empty, so a card turns red only when the link reads exactly `0`. Anything else is up."
      },
      "transparent": true,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "grafana-testdata-datasource",
        "uid": "bdi86bi8f7zswc"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "custom": {
            "aggregation": "last",
            "dateFormat": "YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm:ss",
            "displayAliasType": "Warning / Critical",
            "displayType": "Regular",
            "displayValueWithAlias": "Never",
            "fontFormat": "Bold",
            "thresholds": {
              "valueHandler": "Number Threshold",
              "warn": "",
              "crit": 0
            },
            "valueDisplayRegex": ""
          },
          "mappings": []
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "gridPos": {
